.TH 1986 1 "September 2026" "1986 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
1986 \- Commodore C128DCR emulator
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B 1986
[\fIoptions\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B 1986
is a work-in-progress emulator of the Commodore C128DCR computer. It reuses
the SDL3 display, function-key, and options-overlay conventions of the
sibling projects (1983, 1984, 1985), the Z80 core for CP/M mode, and takes
its 8502 (6502-like) CPU core from the reference VICE SDL port.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-scale\fR N
Window scale factor (1..4). Default 2.
.TP
\fB\-\-fullscreen\fR
Start fullscreen.
.TP
\fB\-\-fast\fR
Run the 8502 at 2 MHz (C128 fast mode).
.TP
\fB\-\-rom\fR DIR
Directory holding the machine ROM images (kernal.rom, basic.rom, chargen.rom).
.TP
\fB\-\-disk\fR PATH
Attach a D64, D71, D81, or read-only standalone PRG at launch.
.TP
\fB\-\-tape\fR PATH
Attach a TAP pulse image or T64 file container at launch.
.TP
\fB\-\-tape\-play\fR
Press Datasette Play on the mounted tape at launch.
.TP
\fB\-\-tape\-play\-at\fR N
Press Datasette Play at emulated frame N.
.TP
\fB\-\-cart\fR PATH
Attach a generic native-C128 CRT or raw external function-ROM image at launch.
.TP
\fB\-\-gif\-out\fR PATH
Start recording an animated GIF at launch.
.TP
\fB\-\-paste\fR TEXT
Inject text through the emulated keyboard.
.TP
\fB\-\-paste\-at\fR N
Delay injected text until emulated frame N.
.TP
\fB\-\-frames\fR N
Exit after N emulated frames.
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-throttle\fR
Run without real-time frame pacing.
.TP
\fB\-\-help\fR
Show this help and exit.
.SH KEYS
.TP
.B F1
Swap host input between C128 joystick ports 1 and 2.
.TP
.B F2
Press or release the Datasette Play button.
.TP
.B F3
Rewind the mounted tape.
.TP
.B F4
Save a PPM screenshot.
.TP
.B F5
Reset.
.TP
.B F6
Toggle animated GIF recording.
.TP
.B F7
Pause/resume.
.TP
.B F8
Monitor.
.TP
.B F9
Open the options overlay (save-and-close with F9, discard with Esc).
.TP
.B F10
Switch between the 40-column VIC-II and 80-column VDC displays.
.TP
.B F11
Toggle fullscreen.
.TP
.B F12
Quit.
.TP
.B Ctrl+V
Paste host clipboard text.
.TP
.B Ctrl++ / Ctrl+-
Adjust window scale.
.TP
.B Shift+Alt
Send C128 Shift+C= to switch between character sets. Caps Lock sends the
same chord if the desktop intercepts Shift+Alt.
.TP
.B Escape / Page Up
C128 RUN/STOP / RESTORE. Press together for RUN/STOP+RESTORE.
.TP
.B Advanced > Keyboard map
Show the host-to-C128 key mappings (enable General > Tinker first).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I 1986.conf
Per-user configuration written by the options overlay.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR SDL3 (3)
.SH BUGS
This is scaffolding: the 8502 core is a subset and the VIC/VDC/CIAs/SID are
stubs. See DEVELOPMENT.md for the roadmap.
